      <p class="/_attributes/common-attributes.md"></p>
      <p>Configure application pods to ensure workload availability during OpenShift Container Platform updates. For example, use deployment strategies, pod disruption budgets, anti-affinity rules, and health probes to maintain high availability and prevent service disruption. In the telecommunications industry, most containerized network function (CNF) vendors follow the guidance in Red Hat best practices for Kubernetes to ensure that the cluster can schedule pods properly during an upgrade.</p>
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Always deploy pods in groups by using <code>Deployment</code> resources. <code>Deployment</code> resources spread the workload across all of the available pods ensuring there is no single point of failure. When a pod that is managed by a <code>Deployment</code> resource is deleted, a new pod takes its place automatically.</p>
